{"name":"Hinoki","hex":"#f8ddb7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hinoki","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tree (species Chamaecyparis obtusa), the Japanese cypress.","The wood of this tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hinoki"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chamaecyparis obtusa","blocks":[{"text":"Chamaecyparis obtusa is a species of conifer in the cypress family, Cupressaceae native to central Japan in East Asia, and widely cultivated in the temperate northern hemisphere for its high-quality timber and ornamental qualities, with many cultivars commercially available.\nIt once existed outside Asia with a range that stretched to Germany during the Miocene. Hinoki grows primarily on the islands of Honshu, Shikoku, and Kyushu. The main massifs are formed in mountainous regions with a moderately humid climate, at altitudes from 300 to 1,500 meters above sea level."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/%E5%A4%A7%E6%99%BA%E5%AF%BA_%28%E5%B2%90%E9%98%9C%E5%B8%82%29-%E6%A8%B9%E9%BD%A2%E7%B4%84700%E5%B9%B4%E3%81%AE%E5%A4%A7%E3%83%92%E3%83%8E%E3%82%ADdaichiji008.jpg/330px-%E5%A4%A7%E6%99%BA%E5%AF%BA_%28%E5%B2%90%E9%98%9C%E5%B8%82%29-%E6%A8%B9%E9%BD%A2%E7%B4%84700%E5%B9%B4%E3%81%AE%E5%A4%A7%E3%83%92%E3%83%8E%E3%82%ADdaichiji008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chamaecyparis_obtusa","wikidata":"Q917187"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Hinoki_cypress_%2871904%29.jpg/500px-Hinoki_cypress_%2871904%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Hinoki_cypress_%2871904%29.jpg/1280px-Hinoki_cypress_%2871904%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Hinoki_cypress_%2871904%29.jpg/500px-Hin